      "description": "Watch Lazio vs Genoa highlights and goals from Serie A on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 30, 2026. A high-stakes Serie A encounter unfolded on August 30, 2026, as Lazio welcomed Genoa to the capital. Both teams displayed immense tactical discipline in a match that kept the spectators on the edge of their seats until the final whistle. Frattesi Breaks the Deadlock The contest began with a cagey atmosphere, but it didn't take long for the hosts to find their rhythm. In the 25th minute, a moment of quality decided the direction of the half. Nuno Tavares delivered a precise assist to Davide Frattesi , who unleashed a clinical left-footed strike to put Lazio ahead. The goal injected energy into the home side, while Genoa struggled to find an immediate answer to the setback. As the first half progressed, tensions began to simmer. Genoa 's Leo Oestigard was shown a yellow card for a robust challenge, and the intensity spread to the touchline. The referee had little patience for dissent, eventually showing a yellow card to Daniele De Rossi as he vocally expressed his frustration. Despite some defensive blunders late in the half, the scoreline remained unchanged heading into the interval. Late Drama and Mandas' Heroics The second half saw a shift in momentum as Genoa pushed hard for an equalizer, controlling 54% of the possession. A series of tactical substitutions followed, with Junior Messias and Milutin Osmajic coming on to bolster the visitors' attack. Lazio retreated into a defensive shell, looking to protect their slender lead while inviting significant pressure from the genovese side. In a frantic finish, the visitors threw everything forward. Osmajic missed a golden opportunity with a header that sailed wide, but the defining moment came in the 94th minute. Christos Mandas produced a stunning save to deny Morten Frendrup 's goal-bound header, ensuring the hosts stayed in front. The match ended with a heated exchange between Mattia Zaccagni and Amorim , resulting in bookings for both, as Lazio held on for a gritty victory."
